---
import SectionTitle from "./SectionTitle.astro";
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<section id="human-control" class="section wrap">
  <SectionTitle
    number="05"
    label="Human-guided AI"
    title="The model suggests. You decide."
  >
    <p>
      Suggest → Confirm → Execute. AI providers hold no mail writer or action
      executor. Permission and execution belong to the application’s controlled
      action layer.
    </p>
  </SectionTitle>
  <ol class="control-flow">
    {[
      ["01", "AI understands", "Context, meaning, and possible next steps."],
      ["02", "AI suggests", "A visible, editable proposal."],
      ["03", "User reviews", "Check the source, scope, and effect."],
      ["04", "User confirms", "Explicit approval for the action."],
      ["05", "Application executes", "Permission checks and a durable record."],
    ].map(([n, title, copy]) => (
      <li class={n === "03" || n === "04" ? "human-step" : ""}>
        <span class="step-number">{n}</span>
        <h3>{title}</h3>
        <p>{copy}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <div class="authority-note">
    <Icon name="lock" size={18} />
    <p>
      <strong>An architectural boundary, by intention.</strong> The assistant is
      read-only. Meaningful external actions require user-defined authority and
      application checks. Remote sends do not offer a fictional Undo.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
